aHq(a,b){return"How much of Total P/L comes from exchange-rate moves rather than the stocks themselves, across your foreign holdings.\n\nTotal P/L is measured in "+a+" against what you paid in "+a+" on each trade date where a dated rate exists. Where none exists, a sell uses the average rate of the holding's buys; anything else uses today's rate, and a note on this card says so. Each holding's own gain or loss (the Locked In and Floating rows when you have partial sells, otherwise just the price move) is measured in its own currency and converted at today's rate. The difference is the currency move on the money you have invested abroad.\n\nFor those holdings: Total P/L = Locked In + Floating + Currency effect \u2212 dividends on shares you have since sold"+b+". Those dividends are inside Locked In, but Total P/L leaves every dividend out, so they are taken back out. All your dividends are under Analysis \u2192 Overview \u2192 Portfolio Quality (Total Dividends Received)."},
gaHr(){return"Current paper gain or loss on the shares you still hold.\n\nThis number changes every time the stock price moves and is only realised when you sell."},
gaHs(){return"Money still at work in your open positions: everything you paid in (buys + commissions) minus what you already got back from any partial sells.\n\nFor positions you have never partially sold, this equals avg buy price \xd7 shares held.\n\nEach trade is converted at the exchange rate of its own date where a dated rate exists, so this number only changes when you buy or sell \u2014 not because of currency movements. Where none exists, a sell uses the average rate of the holding's buys; anything else uses today's rate, and a note on this card says so."},
aHt(a){return"Gain or loss already locked in from shares you have partially sold out of positions you still hold.\n\nThis is money you have actually realised \u2014 it won't change when the stock price moves.\n\nIncludes the dividends paid on the shares you have since sold"+a+", which Total P/L leaves out."},
aHu(a){return" ("+a+" on this card)"},
gaHv(){return"Value-weighted average P/E ratio across your holdings.\n\nP/E = Stock price \xf7 Earnings per share (EPS).\n\nLarger positions have more influence. A higher P/E means the market expects more growth; a lower P/E may indicate the stock is cheap \u2014 or that growth is slow."},
gaHw(){return"P/L %"},
gaHx(){return"Capital gain/loss as a % of what you invested (dividends excluded).\n\nP/L % = Total P/L \xf7 Total Invested\n\nDoes not account for timing \u2014 see Personal IRR in Analysis for that."},
gaHy(){return"The total cash you received from selling these positions, after selling fees (shares \xd7 sell price \u2212 fees).\n\nConverted at today's exchange rates."},
gaHz(){return"Locked-in profit or loss from closed positions, including any dividends received.\n\nRealized P/L = Total Proceeds \u2212 Total Invested + Dividends\n\nConverted at today's exchange rates, so this figure can drift slightly with currency moves after the sale."},
